# Container vulnerability scan exceptions.
#
# Native trivy ignore format, one entry per line:
#
#   CVE-YYYY-#### exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# The comment block directly above an entry records the remediation owner
# and the justification (see docs/image-scanning.md):
#
#   # patched in the next upstream base image digest
#   # owner:@alice
#   CVE-2025-12345 exp:2026-08-01
#
# Rules: only IDs reported by the scan may be listed, each ID at most once,
# and exp must be a valid date at most 90 days out. An expired exception
# stops being ignored and fails the daily scan again.

# CVE-2026-53612/53613/53614: util-linux (libuuid) HIGH findings on the
# python:3.14-alpine base used by images/dagster/hardened/Dockerfile.
# Fixed by util-linux 2.42.3-r0; the pinned base still ships
# libuuid-2.42.1-r0. Renovate bumps the digest when upstream rebuilds;
# drop these entries then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — mount TOCTOU ancestor directory swap
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-11-15
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — nsenter mount namespace TOCTOU, same fix
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-11-15
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — SUID mount nosuid/noexec bypass, same fix
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-76642/78408/78409/78410: util-linux (libuuid) HIGH findings on
# the python:3.14-alpine base used by images/dagster/hardened/Dockerfile.
# Fixed by util-linux 2.42.3-r0; the pinned python:3.14-alpine digest
# still ships libuuid-2.42.1-r0 and no newer digest has been published
# upstream yet (checked 2026-09-05, same digest as `docker pull
# python:3.14-alpine` resolves to today). Renovate bumps the digest when
# upstream rebuilds; drop these entries then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — mount post-hook privileged X-mount.idmap/owner escalation
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — nsenter --join-cgroup root cgroup migration leak, same fix
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — X-mount.subdir detached-tree symlink escape, same fix
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — restricted bind mount owner/group/mode pin bypass, same fix
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-12-04
